.TH CBMAP_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_destroy \- destroy a BST map and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap_destroy(cbm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees all the resources of the BST map. This includes all the nodes,
all the keys and all the values. The macro then sets the map pointer
to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm  BST map to destroy (the macro sets it to NULL after it destroys
     the map)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A call with a NULL pointer is safe

The macro evaluates cbm exactly once. It must be a modifiable lvalue,
such as a variable or an element of an array, so an expression with a
side effect, such as handles[i++], destroys and clears one element.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create (3)
